[% META
   title = "AI Skills and Web Search — v2 design"
   description = "How the v2 AI stack gains DB-backed approval-gated skills and a working, scope-controlled web search. Records why skills live in MariaDB, why search is self-hosted, the search tiers, and what is still pending."
   roles = "admin,developer"
   TemplateType = "Documentation"
   category = "planning,ai"
   page_version = "0.1"
   last_updated = "Wed Sep 10 2026"
   site_specific = "false"
   project_id = "280"
   project_code = "AISYSTEM"
%]
[% PageVersion = 'Documentation/AiSkillsAndWebSearch.tt,v 0.1 2026/09/10 hermes-agent Exp - Skills + web search design' %]
[% IF c.session.debug_mode == 1 %][% PageVersion %][% END %]

<div class="container">
    [% INCLUDE 'admin/documentation/_doc_header.tt'
        page_title   = 'AI Skills and Web Search — v2 design'
        site_name    = site_name
        user_role    = user_role
        last_updated = last_updated
        page_name    = page_name
        doc_project_id   = project_id
        doc_project_code = project_code %]

    <div id="toc" class="row doc-toc">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 class="doc-h2">Quick Navigation</h2>
            <div class="doc-navrow">
                <a href="#summary" class="doc-navlink">Summary</a>
                <a href="#skills" class="doc-navlink">Skills</a>
                <a href="#approval" class="doc-navlink">Approval</a>
                <a href="#search" class="doc-navlink">Web search</a>
                <a href="#why-selfhost" class="doc-navlink">Why self-host</a>
                <a href="#tiers" class="doc-navlink">Tiers</a>
                <a href="#done" class="doc-navlink">Done</a>
                <a href="#pending" class="doc-navlink">Pending</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="summary" class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 class="doc-h2">Summary</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">
                Two capabilities are being added to the v2 AI stack
                (<code>Comserv::Model::AI2::*</code>):
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>Skills</strong> — remembered, reusable ways of doing a
                    recurring AI task, stored in the database and gated behind human
                    approval.</li>
                <li><strong>Web search that works, with controllable scope</strong> —
                    the toggle has never functioned, and hosted APIs cannot limit
                    which sources are searched.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-body">
                v1 (<code>Controller::AI.pm</code>) is dead and out of scope.
                Everything here is v2 only.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="skills" class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 class="doc-h2">Skills — why the database, not a JSON file</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">
                A skills file under <code>root/static/config/</code> would only
                reach production at the next deploy, and each branch mutates its
                own copy independently. Database rows are live on every worktree
                and every site the moment they are approved.
            </p>
            <p class="doc-body">
                Result class:
                <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/AiSkill.pm</code>
                — table <code>ai_skills</code>.
            </p>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr><th>Column</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
                <tr><td><code>skill_key</code></td><td>Stable machine name (unique)</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>trigger_pattern</code></td><td>Matched against the incoming prompt</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>steps</code></td><td>Ordered procedure to follow</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>examples_good</code></td><td>What a correct answer looks like</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>examples_bad</code></td><td>What to avoid — carries most of the weight</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>min_role</code></td><td>Who may invoke it</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>status</code></td><td>pending / approved / rejected</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>source</code></td><td>Provenance — who, when, on what evidence</td></tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-body doc-muted">
                Note: this DBIx::Class build has no working <code>add_index</code>
                (it crashes on reload), so uniqueness is declared with
                <code>add_unique_constraint</code>.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="approval" class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 class="doc-h2">Approval — AI cannot self-authorise a skill</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">
                Skills change how the AI behaves, so an AI-written skill must never
                go live on its own. New rows default to <code>pending</code>, and
                <strong>only <code>approved</code> rows are ever injected into a
                prompt</strong>.
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>Admin</strong> — the AI proposes; the admin approves in
                    chat and it takes effect immediately.</li>
                <li><strong>Everyone else</strong> — the submission is queued and a
                    todo is raised for admin attention.</li>
                <li>Every skill keeps a <code>source</code> value recording who
                    created it, when, and on what evidence, so it stays auditable.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="search" class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 class="doc-h2">Web search — the toggle never worked</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">
                The widget's search checkbox set <code>use_search</code>, and
                <code>Provider/Grok.pm</code> already implemented the matching
                <code>search_parameters</code> — but the flag was dropped between
                them. <code>Chat.pm</code> and <code>Router.pm</code> contained no
                reference to it at all, so the provider always received false.
                <strong>Fixed 2026-09-09</strong> by threading it through the call
                chain as an options hash.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="why-selfhost" class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 class="doc-h2">Why self-hosted search</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">
                The requirement is to control the <em>extent</em> of a search — for
                example, ENCY looking up herbal remedies should be able to search
                European and traditional sources rather than only the North
                American medical industry.
            </p>
            <p class="doc-body">
                Measured 2026-09-09: OpenRouter's
                <code>web_search_options.search_domain_filter</code> is
                <strong>silently ignored</strong>. A strict
                <code>["en.wikipedia.org"]</code> filter returned 16 sources with
                <strong>zero</strong> from Wikipedia — identical to the unfiltered
                control, while still billing. Hosted APIs therefore cannot deliver
                scope control, so the <code>free</code> tier is a service we run:
                <code>comserv2-search</code> (SearXNG), defined in
                <code>services/search/</code> and reached via a full URL in
                <code>root/config/services.json</code>.
            </p>
            <p class="doc-body doc-muted">
                SearXNG is a <em>metasearch</em> aggregator, not a web index — it
                fans out to upstream engines that are explicitly enabled in
                <code>settings.yml</code>. Commercial engines (Google, Bing, Brave,
                Startpage) ship disabled; enable them only if you accept that
                queries go to them.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="tiers" class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 class="doc-h2">Search tiers</h2>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr><th>Tier</th><th>Backend</th><th>Cost</th><th>Who</th></tr>
                <tr><td><code>internal</code></td><td>MariaDB full text over documentation / ENCY</td><td>free</td><td>everyone</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>free</code></td><td>self-hosted <code>comserv2-search</code></td><td>free</td><td>default</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>cheap</code></td><td><code>perplexity/sonar</code> via OpenRouter</td><td>~$0.005/query</td><td>admin, developer</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>best</code></td><td>Grok native search</td><td>quota-bound</td><td>admin, developer</td></tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-body">
                Programming questions are <strong>searched live, never indexed</strong>
                — crawling and storing programming documentation would waste
                resources on an already-solved problem.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="done" class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 class="doc-h2">Done</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><code>use_search</code> threaded through <code>Chat.pm</code> and
                    <code>Router.pm</code> — verified 4/4.</li>
                <li>Grok quota 403 no longer reported as an expired login
                    (<code>Grok.pm</code>, <code>Router.pm</code>,
                    <code>Admin/Git.pm</code>).</li>
                <li><code>AiSkill</code> Result class written and registered —
                    DBIC resolves <code>ai_skills</code>.</li>
                <li><code>AI2::Search</code> client written — verified 16/16,
                    including that a disabled service issues no request.</li>
                <li><code>services/search/</code> scaffold plus a
                    <code>services.json</code> entry shipping
                    <code>enabled: 0</code>.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="pending" class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 class="doc-h2">Pending</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>Create the <code>ai_skills</code> table</strong> —
                    todo <strong>#2430</strong>. Admin action via in-app
                    schema-compare; never hand-written DDL. This belongs to the
                    <code>schema</code> branch.</li>
                <li><strong>Build and start the search container</strong> —
                    <code>cd services/search &amp;&amp; docker compose up -d --build</code>,
                    then set <code>enabled: 1</code>.</li>
                <li>Skill loader and write-back (blocked on the table).</li>
                <li>Tool registry: register existing capabilities behind one
                    dispatch table.</li>
                <li>Context engineering: world/constraint blocks and per-agent bad
                    examples.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

</div>
